-- title:
--   Triviality of Pic⁰ in characteristic ℓ for genus-zero X₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and suppose that `JZero p` is a subsingleton, that is, that the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$p$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ — the quotient of the degree-zero divisors of `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ of the full level-$p$ modular function field inside Laurent series, by the subgroup of principal degree-zero divisors — has at most one element. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \nmid p$, and let $A'$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ satisfying `LiesOverPrime ℓ`, i.e. the image of $\ell$ in $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ is a non-unit of $A'$. Then `JZeroC (ResidueField A') p` is a subsingleton: the degree-zero divisor class group of the characteristic-$\ell$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFullC (ResidueField A') p`, the subextension of the Laurent series field over the residue field of $A'$ generated by `divisorExpansionsC` at level $p$, has at most one element.
--
--   This is the statement that an $X_0(p)$ of genus zero has trivial degree-zero divisor class group after reduction at any prime $\ell$ not dividing $p$, the genus being unchanged away from $p$. It supplies the triviality hypothesis used by [`ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronIdentityComponentGood`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_jZeroNeronIdentityComponentGood).
